      "id": "jvb8yqu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Banking"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) was established on April 1, 1935, under the RBI Act, 1934, based on the Hilton Young Commission recommendations.",
        "Commercial banks are broadly categorized into Scheduled Banks (listed in the 2nd Schedule of the RBI Act, 1934) and Non-Scheduled Banks.",
        "Monetary policy instruments include quantitative tools (CRR, SLR, Repo Rate, MSF) and qualitative tools (moral suasion, credit rationing).",
        "Modern digital banking architecture relies heavily on NPCI products, including UPI, IMPS, RTGS, and NEFT for seamless payment settlement."
      ],
      "id": "gb1se7n"
    },
