    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "RBI nationalisation took place on January 1, 1949; 14 major private banks were nationalised in 1969, and 6 more in 1980.",
        "Minimum capital requirement for Scheduled Commercial Banks is ₹5 Lakhs under Section 42(6)(a) of the RBI Act, 1934.",
        "RTGS operates on a real-time gross settlement basis with a minimum transfer threshold of ₹2 Lakhs, whereas NEFT has no minimum limit."
      ],
